## REVIEW — Pre-PR Infrastructure Check

Run before every PR. Read all `.tf` files under `_modules/` and `environments/`, then check every item below.

### Wrapper-module pattern

- **BLOCKING:** `environments/*/main.tf` must never call `source = "clouddrove/*/aws"` directly — only `source = "../../_modules/<name>"`
- **BLOCKING:** Every `_modules/<name>/main.tf` must start with a `module "labels"` call to `../_modules/labels` — no module may define its own `name_prefix` locals
- **BLOCKING:** `_modules/labels` outputs `name_prefix` (`{client}-{env}`) and `tags` — all downstream modules must consume these outputs, never recompute them

### labels module usage

Every wrapper module must follow this pattern:

```hcl
module "labels" {
  source         = "../labels"
  client_name    = var.client_name
  environment    = var.environment
  repository_url = var.repository_url
  cost_center    = var.cost_center
}

locals {
  np = module.labels.name_prefix   # e.g. "acme-prod"
}
```

- **BLOCKING:** Missing `module "labels"` call in any `_modules/*/main.tf`
- **ADVISORY:** Direct `"${var.client_name}-${var.environment}"` string construction instead of `module.labels.name_prefix`

### Naming convention

All resources must follow `{client_name}-{environment}-{resource}`. Verify:

- EKS cluster name = `${local.np}-eks`
- WAF Web ACL name = `${local.np}-waf`
- ALB name = `${local.np}-alb`
- Aurora cluster = `${local.np}-aurora`
- ElastiCache replication group = `${local.np}-redis`
- CloudWatch dashboard = `${local.np}-ops`
- KMS key aliases = `alias/${local.np}-{domain}` (rds / eks / s3 / app)
- Secrets Manager = `${local.np}/{service}/master`

- **BLOCKING:** Any resource name that doesn't derive from `module.labels.name_prefix`

### Security controls

- **BLOCKING:** KMS encryption missing on Aurora, ElastiCache, EKS etcd, S3, or Secrets Manager
- **BLOCKING:** `publicly_accessible = true` on Aurora
- **BLOCKING:** `transit_encryption_enabled = false` on ElastiCache
- **BLOCKING:** ALB listener missing TLS (port 443) or missing HTTP→HTTPS redirect
- **BLOCKING:** WAF not associated with ALB (`waf_acl_arn` not passed to alb module)
- **BLOCKING:** `enable_dns_validation = false` in ACM without a matching `aws_route53_record` + `aws_acm_certificate_validation` resource
- **ADVISORY:** EKS public endpoint enabled in prod (`endpoint_public_access = true`)
- **ADVISORY:** Aurora `performance_insights_enabled = false` in prod

### CloudDrove WAF module gotchas

- **BLOCKING:** `waf_scop` (not `waf_scope`) — the upstream CloudDrove variable name is missing the 'e'; using `waf_scope` silently has no effect
- **BLOCKING:** `web_acl_association = true` inside the WAF module — association must be done by the ALB module, not the WAF module, to avoid a circular dependency
- **ADVISORY:** `allow_default_action = true` means requests not matching any rule are allowed — set `false` only after validating no legitimate traffic is blocked

### ACM + DNS ordering

- **BLOCKING:** `module "acm"` called with `zone_id` hardcoded instead of `zone_id = module.dns.zone_id` — this breaks automatic cert validation
- **BLOCKING:** `subject_alternative_names` passed to `module "dns"` — SANs belong to `module "acm"`, not the DNS module
- **ADVISORY:** `enable_dns_validation = false` without explanation — this is correct for the CloudDrove pattern (explicit record creation) but should be documented

### Module versioning

- **BLOCKING:** Any `_modules/*/main.tf` calling a CloudDrove module without a pinned `version =` constraint
- **BLOCKING:** Using a git ref or branch instead of a registry version
- **ADVISORY:** Outdated version — compare against current upstream; check known bug status

### Known upstream bugs (AWS provider v5)

Three CloudDrove modules use `data.aws_region.*.region` (removed in AWS provider v5 — should be `data.aws_region.current.name`). After `terraform init`, patch the downloaded source:

```bash
for dir in \
  .terraform/modules/vpc \
  .terraform/modules/waf \
  .terraform/modules/eks_addons/modules/karpenter; do
  [ -d "$dir" ] && \
    find "$dir" -name "*.tf" -exec \
      sed -i '' 's/data\.aws_region\.\*\.region/data.aws_region.current.name/g' {} \;
done
```

Issues filed: [terraform-aws-vpc#105](https://github.com/clouddrove/terraform-aws-vpc/issues/105), [terraform-aws-waf#113](https://github.com/clouddrove/terraform-aws-waf/issues/113), [terraform-aws-eks-addons#200](https://github.com/clouddrove/terraform-aws-eks-addons/issues/200)

### Variables and outputs

- **BLOCKING:** Any `variable` block without a `description`
- **BLOCKING:** Any `output` block without a `description`
- **BLOCKING:** Passwords, tokens, or keys in outputs without `sensitive = true`
- **ADVISORY:** Variables without `type`

### Backend

- **BLOCKING:** No `backend "s3"` block with `dynamodb_table` for state locking
- **BLOCKING:** Different `key` per environment — each environment must have a unique state key

### Review output format

```
BLOCKING — Must fix before merge
---------------------------------
[_modules/waf/main.tf:45]  CC6.6: WAF not associated with ALB — pass waf_acl_arn to alb module
[_modules/aurora/main.tf:12]  C1.1: Missing kms_key_id on Aurora cluster

ADVISORY — Should fix
----------------------
[environments/prod/main.tf:88]  CC6.7: EKS public endpoint enabled in prod

SOC2/GDPR: 2 blocking (CC6.6, C1.1), 1 advisory. Fix blocking before raising PR.
```

