## NEW — Scaffold a Module

### Identify module type

Extract from argument (e.g. `new monitoring`, `new s3`). If not provided, ask: "Which module? (security / vpc / eks / aurora / elasticache / alb / dns / acm / waf / iam / monitoring / s3 / secrets / dashboard / labels)"

### Standard variable set

Every `_modules/<name>/variables.tf` must include these four variables — copy verbatim:

```hcl
variable "client_name"    { type = string; description = "Client slug — used as resource name prefix." }
variable "environment"    {
  type        = string
  description = "Deployment environment."
  validation {
    condition     = contains(["dev", "staging", "prod", "sandbox"], var.environment)
    error_message = "Must be dev, staging, prod, or sandbox."
  }
}
variable "repository_url" { type = string; description = "Source repository URL — applied as a tag." }
variable "cost_center"    { type = string; description = "Cost center code — applied as a tag." }
```

### Standard `main.tf` header

Every `_modules/<name>/main.tf` must start with:

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.6.0"
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
  }
}

module "labels" {
  source         = "../labels"
  client_name    = var.client_name
  environment    = var.environment
  repository_url = var.repository_url
  cost_center    = var.cost_center
}

locals {
  np = module.labels.name_prefix
}
```

### CloudDrove module call pattern

```hcl
module "<name>" {
  source  = "clouddrove/<name>/aws"
  version = "<pinned-version>"

  name        = "${local.np}-<suffix>"
  environment = var.environment
  label_order = ["name"]

  tags = module.labels.tags
  # ... module-specific variables
}
```

Always set `label_order = ["name"]` — this ensures the upstream CloudDrove module uses only the `name` attribute for its own internal naming, not appending environment again (which would produce `acme-prod-prod-eks`).

### Generated files

Produce three files in `_modules/<name>/`:

**`variables.tf`** — standard four vars + module-specific vars, all with `description` and `type`

**`main.tf`** — `terraform {}` block + `module "labels"` + `locals { np }` + the CloudDrove module call with `name = "${local.np}-<suffix>"`, `label_order = ["name"]`, `tags = module.labels.tags`

**`outputs.tf`** — all IDs, ARNs, names; each with `description`; secrets with `sensitive = true`

